cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hybrid-H1: Computational Design of a Modular Nanoparticle Platform for α-Synuclein Oligomer Targeting"
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the associated Hybrid-H1 manuscript and this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Topno"
    given-names: "Abhishek"
year: 2026
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - Parkinson's disease
  - alpha-synuclein
  - aptamer
  - F5R2
  - nanoparticle
  - molecular docking
  - molecular dynamics
  - computational drug design
abstract: >
  Computational proof-of-concept project describing Hybrid-H1, a modular
  nanoparticle platform designed for targeted recognition of alpha-synuclein
  oligomers using an engineered F5R2 aptamer, auxiliary peptide recognition,
  RVG29, trehalose, and a PLGA nanoparticle core.
repository-code: https://github.com/Abhishek499-lab/Parkinson-Nanoparticle
